# Capstone_Android — Kotlin + Jetpack Compose, two Gradle modules (:app, :extractor).
# Capstone_Android is a subfolder of the repo rooted at the project folder, so the
# root .gitignore applies here too. This file keeps the rules that are specific
# to the Android project.

# ---- Gradle / build output -------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
/build
app/build/
extractor/build/
.kotlin/
.cxx
.externalNativeBuild
captures/

# ---- Machine-specific: SDK path, toolchain pin -----------------------------
# local.properties holds this machine's sdk.dir.
local.properties
# gradle-daemon-jvm.properties pins the daemon to whatever JDK this machine
# happens to have (here, the JetBrains runtime). Committing it makes the build
# fail on any machine without that exact JDK.
gradle/gradle-daemon-jvm.properties

# ---- IDE churn -------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml

# ---- Build artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab

# ---- Model weights ---------------------------------------------------------
# 570 MB / 810 MB / 1.7 GB. These live outside the repo and are pushed to the
# device with `adb push` into /data/local/tmp/llm (see RUNBOOK.md).
*.litertlm

# ---- OS cruft --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Deliberately TRACKED --------------------------------------------------
# The ArUco fixture page and its layout are the only real test worksheet in the
# project; GoldenSampleTest, MarkerContractTest and PageExtractorTest all read
# them. Nothing above matches this path — these lines exist so that a future
# `*.png` or `*.json` rule cannot silently drop it.
!extractor/src/test/resources/sample/
!extractor/src/test/resources/sample/**
